films.push({"id":"the-word-came-alive","title":"The Word Came Alive","creator":"Moving Works","runtime":"01:59","language":"English","kind":"Documentary testimony","tags":["Faith","Hope"],"summary":"Nate and Ruth reflect on grieving the loss of their newborn daughter and finding strength in Scripture while serving in Brazil. A two-minute short derived from Blessed.","contentNote":"Discusses a newborn not breathing, infant death, a funeral and intense parental grief. The couple share their personal Christian response to loss, not medical advice, a promise of recovery or a standard for how anyone should grieve.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VjGONVMo4aY","source":"https://movingworks.org/films/the-word-came-alive","thumbnailSource":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/68e6c536afd77c2cc03e6998/699de8f48492ba69dac40f60_The-Word-Came-Alive-WF.jpg","checked":"2026-11-08","checkedDisplay":"8 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Official Moving Works page embeds this exact upload and labels the unsubtitled original English. Full authored English transcript reviewed0:03-1:45. Exact119.978seconds, displayed1:59 after loading; creator describes a two-minute short derived from Blessed. Original non-ad opening, middle, closing and ended state checked8November2026.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
films.push({"id":"adopted","title":"Adopted","creator":"Moving Works","runtime":"08:44","language":"English","kind":"Documentary testimony","tags":["Faith","Family","Love"],"summary":"After a three-and-a-half-year wait, Peter and Erin travel to Ethiopia to meet their daughter Tirfe. Their family story is interwoven with Scripture about being welcomed into God's family.","contentNote":"Discusses loss of a birth mother, early childhood adversity and separation from an original family. Includes emotionally loaded orphan language, Christian sin and salvation imagery, and the parents' personal adoption perspective. A historical testimony, not current adoption guidance or a claim that adoption erases grief.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-iaCFZ-RuUw","source":"https://movingworks.org/films/adopted","thumbnailSource":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/68e6c536afd77c2cc03e6998/699ddbc54ec0651359019f6a_Adopted-WF.jpg","checked":"2026-11-08","checkedDisplay":"8 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Official Moving Works page embeds this exact upload and labels the unsubtitled original English. Full authored English transcript reviewed0:03-8:25. Loaded player duration524.561seconds displays8:44; initial rounded metadata gives525seconds. Original non-ad opening, middle, closing and ended state checked8November2026.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
films.push({"id":"beginning-of-holiness","title":"Beginning of Holiness","creator":"Outside da Box / Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston","runtime":"01:46","language":"English","kind":"Documentary short","tags":["Faith","Prayer","Love","Service"],"summary":"Mother Teresa reflects on listening to God in prayer and how faith can lead to love, service and peace. Images of a tin-can telephone and hand-lettered words accompany this short Catholic VCAT reflection.","contentNote":"A prayer reflection, not a narrative drama. Uses archival Mother Teresa audio, credited in the film to the documentary Mother Teresa: The Legacy.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WupB22jXUcY","source":"https://www.odbfilms.com/","thumbnailSource":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/WupB22jXUcY/maxresdefault.webp","checked":"2026-11-09","checkedDisplay":"9 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Current ODB Films homepage links its Prayer collection to this exact ODB Films upload. English speech, on-screen text and full transcript reviewed0:23-1:25. Exact106.221seconds, player1:46. Opening, middle, closing credits and original non-ad ended state checked9November2026. Directed by Cory Heimann; edited by JP Talty; hand lettering by Marie Heimann.","number":72,"image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
films.push({"id":"the-green-rubber-band","title":"The Green Rubber Band","creator":"Outside da Box / Spirit Juice Studios / Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston","runtime":"05:50","language":"English","kind":"Documentary testimony","tags":["Faith","Prayer","Hope","Trust"],"summary":"Lesley recalls a camp keepsake, a difficult mountain hike with her brother and the moment a green rubber band became a personal sign of hope and surrender to God. A testimony from the Catholic VCAT series.","contentNote":"Discusses a head injury, brain injury and relearning everyday skills, followed by an injured hiker in severe pain. The meaning Lesley finds in the rubber band is her personal faith interpretation, not medical or wilderness-safety advice.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s3XFtTTidHc","source":"https://www.odbfilms.com/","thumbnailSource":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/s3XFtTTidHc/maxresdefault.webp","checked":"2026-11-09","checkedDisplay":"9 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Current ODB Films homepage links its Prayer collection to this exact ODB Films upload. Upload description credits Outside da Box and Spirit Juice Studios in collaboration with the Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston. Full English transcript reviewed0:09-5:47. Exact350.181seconds, player5:50; playlist rounds to5:51. Original non-ad opening, middle, closing and ended state checked9November2026.","number":73,"image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
films.push({"id":"the-23rd-psalm","title":"The 23rd Psalm","creator":"Stewart H. Redwine / 36 Parables / Outside da Box","runtime":"01:34","language":"English","kind":"Scripture film","tags":["Prayer","Trust","Hope","Scripture"],"summary":"Psalm 23 unfolds through torn paper, drawings and stop-motion imagery, from green pastures to the dark valley and the promise of dwelling with God. A short, text-led Scripture film by Stewart H. Redwine of 36 Parables, shared by Outside da Box.","contentNote":"English on-screen Scripture rather than a dialogue drama. Includes references to death, evil and enemies, with dark and burning-paper imagery.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U89I_Sb87Wo","source":"https://www.odbfilms.com/","thumbnailSource":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/U89I_Sb87Wo/maxresdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAKENAF8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-CYAC0AWKAgwIABABGGUgWyhSMA8=&rs=AOn4CLAhqjFGtGnWNNW6BnA5JnDK1qYXgA","checked":"2026-11-09","checkedDisplay":"9 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Current ODB Films homepage links its Prayer collection to this exact official ODB Films upload. Upload description credits producer Stewart H. Redwine of 36 Parables. English on-screen Psalm text and original opening, middle and closing imagery reviewed. Exact94.458774seconds, player1:34; playlist rounds to1:35. Original non-ad playback and ended state verified9November2026.","number":74,"image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});

films.push({"id":"prayer","title":"Prayer","creator":"Outside da Box / Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston","runtime":"02:58","language":"English","kind":"Documentary testimony","tags":["Prayer","Faith","Gratitude"],"summary":"Teenagers from the Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston describe prayer as a personal conversation with God. They talk about gratitude, busy routines, praying around friends and asking Mary to pray with them in this short VCAT reflection.","contentNote":"A Catholic documentary reflection, not a narrative drama. Includes the Hail Mary and references to Mary praying with and for believers; the teenagers describe their own prayer habits and beliefs.","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kTnFPDQpTuI","source":"https://www.odbfilms.com/","thumbnailSource":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/kTnFPDQpTuI/maxresdefault.webp","checked":"2026-11-09","checkedDisplay":"9 November 2026","runtimeEvidence":"Current ODB Films homepage links its Prayer collection to this exact official upload. Upload description and closing copyright card credit Outside da Box and the Diocese of Wheeling-Charleston. Full English interview transcript, opening and closing cards reviewed. Exact178.221seconds, player2:58; playlist rounds to2:59. Original non-ad playback and ended state verified9November2026.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
